      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $(2a+1)({a}^{2}+a+10)?$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute both terms of the binomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2a+1)({a}^{2}+a+10) & = \\\\ 2a({a}^{2}+a+10)+1({a}^{2}+a+10) & = \\\\ 2{a}^{3}+2{a}^{2}+20a+{a}^{2}+a+10 & = \\\\ 2{a}^{3}+3{a}^{2}+21a+10\\end{aligned}\n$$",
